## Consent register

The filmmaker's story is about his father. The conversation does not establish that recorded informed consent has been obtained for use of the father's identifiable face, likeness, or voice. Therefore, do not generate or publish an identifiable likeness or cloned voice unless consent is obtained and recorded.

| Person/identifier | Use (face / likeness / voice) | Consent status | Date | Evidence location | Scope confirmed |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Filmmaker's father | No identifiable likeness or voice planned; use a generic, non-identifiable illustrative character only unless permission is later documented. | Not established for identifiable use; do not use identifiable face/voice. | [IF LATER OBTAINED] | [SECURE PRIVATE RECORD, IF APPLICABLE] | [CONFIRM SCOPE BEFORE IDENTIFIABLE USE] |

If the plan changes to include identifiable photographs, footage, likeness, or voice, obtain recorded, informed consent first and update this table. The narrator must not imitate the father's voice.

